id: pm-tgw0ir
title: "Read paths that render outside the contracted delivery stage bypass --output-budget: direct context/next markdown renders, output_format services rendering before row projection, and custom renderers that grow after a receipt-free fit check"
description: "CodeRabbit review of PR 1681 (deferred as heavy-lift or a poor tradeoff for that batch). (1) 'pm context --for orient --output-budget 1 --format markdown' renders directly in src/cli/register-list-query.ts and emits more than the budget with exit 0, so the direct-render paths need the same accounting and refusal as formatEffectiveOutput. (2) When an output_format service renders a two-row result under --output-limit 1, the audit measures the projected one-row result while the CLI may emit the service's two-row string. The projected result should be rendered through the service and the resulting string audited. (3) A renderer can grow after a receipt-free fit check, or add substantive output when token_accounting is attached, so the final substantive output should be verified against the budget and receipts excluding receipt overhead, with a native fallback, while unbounded custom rendering is preserved."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,budget,read-output,token-efficiency
